WEBVTT

00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:13,780
What is our EMF waves less harmful than x-rays?

00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,700
Well, most certainly, I would say, yes.

00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:26,220
So, EMFs are electromagnetic frequency,

00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,900
x-rays are also electromagnetic frequency,

00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,260
so x-ray are extremely damaging to the tissue.

00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,700
But, of course, you have to weigh all that out.

00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:40,780
So, if I have x-rays that you have to do for my teeth,

00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:45,060
what's the rad dose of those x-rays,

00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:49,940
but not very high?

00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:52,580
So, I could probably do, I don't know,

00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:57,420
52 x-rays equivalent to one chest x-ray.

00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:00,180
Chest x-rays typically, which you compare things to,

00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:02,500
because as far as an x-ray itself,

00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:05,300
a plane, let's call the plane view x-ray,

00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,300
which is the old days when you took a x-ray,

00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:12,700
you had a physical x-ray in front of you,

00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:17,700
well, we don't see that so much, we see it's all digital,

00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:22,260
but it would always compare to a chest x-ray,

00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:23,860
because it's about a radiation that was needed

00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:25,180
for a chest x-ray.

00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:27,620
Well, if you have to go and get two x-rays,

00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:29,980
I don't know how many two x-rays are gonna equivalent

00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:32,900
rad dose of a chest x-ray.

00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:36,740
Compare that to a PET scan or a CT scan.

00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:39,020
So, let's have to do a CT scan in my lumbar spine

00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:40,980
because I hurt my mac really bad.

00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:44,980
But CT scan is equivalent to about 50 chest x-rays.

00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:48,260
So, again, it's the rad dose of the radiation

00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:49,820
that you're concerned with.

00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:52,740
And yeah, EMF radiation is bad too.

00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,580
So, if I'm using my cell phone

00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:56,300
and I got it up to my head all the time,

00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:58,820
talking like this, I never recommend that.

00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,420
You know, that EMF's are going right through your head.

00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,220
It's the constant use of it.

00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:07,500
So, what's the rad dose over time is really the question.

00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:11,220
So, yeah, there's a different issue there.

